        "cinderfall": {
            "tagline": "Every raging spirit is grieving something, and every haunted engine is still following an order nobody countermanded. Find the wound, and the monster stops being a monster for exactly as long as it takes to end it — or end its suffering instead.",
            "role": "Exorcist / Anchor-Hunter",
            "pillar": "Combat — Spiritual Faith turned to hunting, not worship",
            "hpFormula": "8 + Con / level",
            "keyAbilityText": "Intelligence",
            "terms": [
                [
                    "The Ward",
                    "Your bound relic — Blade, Lantern, Chain, or Mirror — carries a fragment of captured spirit-static and channels every anchor-rite you perform. Chosen at 1st level; it can be stolen, but never simply lost."
                ],
                [
                    "Anchor",
                    "The unresolved grief, trauma, or corrupted directive that keeps a raging spirit or hostile ghost-machine locked into violence instead of dissipating naturally. Every hostile haunting has exactly one, however deep it's buried."
                ],
                [
                    "Static",
                    "Your inborn early-warning sense — a prickle at the back molars, a hiss under the ears — that flares near an Anchor-bound hostile. Passive by default; can be focused deliberately into Naming an Anchor."
                ],
                [
                    "Name the Anchor",
                    "The act of reading a hostile spirit or ghost-machine closely enough to identify its Anchor. Success Names it for the rest of the encounter, unlocking your Ward's signature Break effect against that target specifically."
                ],
                [
                    "Break the Anchor",
                    "Your Ward's answer to a Named target — different for every Ward, from a blade that cuts straight past the rage to the grief underneath, to a chain offering the spirit a way to stop that isn't dissolution."
                ],
                [
                    "Ward-Scrawled Charm",
                    "A one-use chalk-and-ash sigil, prepared before you head out and torn or burned in the field for an immediate esoteric effect. You know a small repertoire and can only carry so many at once."
                ]
            ],
